{"id":6505,"date":"2026-09-23T10:30:00","date_gmt":"2026-09-23T09:30:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.jouwweb.nl\/blog\/?p=6505"},"modified":"2026-08-19T11:42:38","modified_gmt":"2026-08-19T10:42:38","slug":"eu-ai-act-do-you-need-to-label-ai-content-on-your-website","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.webador.com\/blog\/eu-ai-act-do-you-need-to-label-ai-content-on-your-website\/","title":{"rendered":"Do You Need to Label AI Content on Your Website?"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Artificial Intelligence has become an essential tool for website owners. Whether you are using ChatGPT to craft the perfect &#8220;About Us&#8221; page or <a href=\"https:\/\/www.midjourney.com\/explore?tab=top\">Midjourney<\/a> to generate a stunning header image, AI tools save time and money. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">However, as of August 2, 2026, new transparency rules have officially taken effect under the <strong>EU AI Act (the European Union&#8217;s Artificial Intelligence Act)<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Does this mean you now have to put a warning label on every single sentence written by ChatGPT? The short answer is: <strong>No!<\/strong> So what should you actually look out for?<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">At Webador, we have summarized exactly what the new AI labeling requirements mean for your website and how you can easily stay compliant.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:70px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Biggest Myth: &#8220;All AI Content Must Be Labeled&#8221;<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Let&#8217;s clear up a widespread misconception right away: There is <strong>no blanket labeling requirement<\/strong> for all AI-generated content. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The core goal of the EU AI Act is to prevent users from being deceived online. Visitors should be able to tell whether they are interacting with a human or a machine, especially when it comes to sensitive topics. Therefore, the rules depend entirely on your specific use case.<br><\/p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:50px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What Actually Needs an AI Label (And What Doesn&#8217;t)<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">As a website owner, blogger, or small business, there are three main categories of AI content you need to monitor:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>1. Images, Video, and Audio <\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you publish images, videos, or audio content that has been entirely generated or significantly altered by AI (often referred to as &#8220;deepfakes&#8221;), <strong>you must clearly label them<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Example:<\/strong> A photorealistic image in your blog post that you generated using Midjourney, DALL-E, or Stable Diffusion.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Exception:<\/strong> If you only used AI tools to adjust the brightness of a real photograph, remove a background, or retouch minor blemishes, you do not need to label it.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>2. Texts and Blog Posts <\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This is where most website owners can breathe a sigh of relief. According to the EU guidelines, AI-generated text generally <strong>only needs a label<\/strong> if two conditions are met simultaneously:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>The text covers matters of <strong>public interest<\/strong> (e.g., hard news, politics, societal issues, medical advice).<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>The text was published <strong>without significant human oversight<\/strong> (editorial review).<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>The good news:<\/strong> For everyday e-commerce product descriptions, standard marketing copy, translations, or grammar corrections, this labeling obligation usually <em>does not apply<\/em>.<br><\/p>\n\n\n\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Pro Tip<\/strong> \ud83d\udca1 &#8211;  Always review AI content before it goes live. If you take a draft from ChatGPT, fact-check it, edit it, and adapt it to your own brand voice. This way you are taking editorial responsibility. In most cases, this removes the need for an AI label!<\/p>\n<\/blockquote>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>3. AI Chatbots and Customer Service<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Have you integrated an automated AI chatbot on your website to handle customer support? If so, you must inform your visitors that they are chatting with a machine\u2014unless it is very obvious from the context.<br><\/p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:50px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What About Webador&#8217;s Built-In Features and Image Gallery?<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You might be wondering about the content you get directly through our platform. Here is how the EU AI Act applies to Webador&#8217;s specific features:<br><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The Webador Image Gallery: <\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The free stock images available in our built-in gallery are standard, royalty-free photographs. You <strong>do not need to add an AI label<\/strong> to these images, as they are real stock photos, not AI-generated deepfakes.<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"933\" height=\"650\" src=\"https:\/\/www.jouwweb.nl\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/Screenshot-2026-08-06-at-12.11.07.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-6506\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.webador.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/Screenshot-2026-08-06-at-12.11.07.png 933w, https:\/\/www.webador.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/Screenshot-2026-08-06-at-12.11.07-300x209.png 300w, https:\/\/www.webador.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/Screenshot-2026-08-06-at-12.11.07-768x535.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 933px) 100vw, 933px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Webador AI Text Generation: <\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you use Webador&#8217;s built-in AI features to draft text for your website, the same &#8220;Text&#8221; rules mentioned above apply. Since you are using it to build typical website pages (like your homepage or services page) and reviewing the text before hitting publish, you take on editorial responsibility and generally do not need to label it.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:50px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How to Label AI Content Correctly in Practice<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The EU does not demand complex technical watermarks from everyday website owners. The law simply requires <strong>clear and understandable information<\/strong>. Here is how you can easily implement this on your site:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>For Images:<\/strong> Add a short note directly in the image caption or alt text (e.g., <em>&#8220;Image source: AI-generated via Midjourney&#8221;<\/em>).<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>For Texts (if required):<\/strong> Place a simple sentence at the bottom of the article (e.g., <em>&#8220;This article was drafted with the assistance of Artificial Intelligence.&#8221;<\/em>).<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>General Transparency:<\/strong> Adding a brief transparency statement to your Imprint (Legal Notice) or Privacy Policy page is always a smart, future-proof idea.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:50px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What Are the Penalties for Non-Compliance?<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While the EU AI Act theoretically includes massive fines, the real danger for small website owners and freelancers comes from a different direction: <strong>warnings from competitors<\/strong>. If you secretly use AI-generated content to gain an unfair competitive advantage, you make yourself vulnerable to legal cease-and-desist letters. A quick transparency note saves you a lot of legal headaches.<br><\/p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:50px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Conclusion: Keep Building Your Website Without Panic<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can absolutely continue using AI tools to make your Webador website look and sound professional. As long as you use AI as a creative assistant to shape your ideas and manually review the results, you are on the safe side. It&#8217;s important to add a transparent label for completely AI-generated photos, automated chatbots, or unedited news articles.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:40px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em><strong>Disclaimer:<\/strong> This article is for informational purposes only and does not constitute legal advice. If you have complex legal questions regarding your specific website, we recommend consulting a qualified attorney.<\/em><\/p>\n<\/blockquote>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-light-gray-background-color has-background\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-not-stacked-on-mobile is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 